// Cloudflare Workers configuration for the live site, on the Workers FREE plan.
//
// Two halves, one Worker:
//
//  * `/`, `/account/` and `/games/<slug>/` are static assets served by
//    Cloudflare's asset router. `run_worker_first` is scoped to `/api/*`, so a
//    game page never invokes a line of code - and static asset requests are
//    free and unlimited on the Free plan.
//  * `/api/*` invokes the tiny Worker script (`edge/src/router.js`), which
//    proxies the request to the Rust service on Google Cloud Run. The service's
//    URL lives in `API_BASE_URL` below; the front-door secret is a Worker secret
//    set with `wrangler secret put API_DOOR_SECRET` and is never written here.
//
// The Free plan allows 100,000 Worker requests a day, and only the `/api/*`
// requests count: the games are served by the asset router and keep loading even
// when that daily cap is reached. That is the fail-open rule in practice.
//
// The custom domain (play2learn.divanchyshyn.com) is deliberately absent: it is
// attached once in the Cloudflare dashboard, which keeps account and domain
// details out of the repository. Keeping the Worker's name `learn-and-play` is
// what keeps that domain attached.
//
// API_BASE_URL is filled in once, from
//   gcloud run services describe learn-and-play-api --region us-central1
//     --format='value(status.url)'
// (docs/backend/RUNBOOK.md, R6/R7). Empty means "not configured yet": `/api/*`
// answers 503 with `api_unconfigured`, and the games are unaffected.
{
  "name": "learn-and-play",
  "main": "edge/src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-20",

  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*"]
  },

  "vars": {
    "API_BASE_URL": ""
  },

  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
